  "articleBody": "Installing a walk-in shower can seem straightforward, but there are a few common pitfalls that can turn your dream bathroom into a nightmare. Knowing these can help you avoid costly mistakes and ensure your new shower is a joy for years to come. One big one is poor waterproofing. Seriously, this is critical! If the waterproofing isn't done perfectly, you're looking at potential water damage, mold, and big repair bills. Always make sure every seam and corner is properly sealed, and give sealants plenty of time to cure. Another mistake is incorrect drain alignment or slope. Water needs to flow efficiently to the drain, and if it doesn’t, you’ll have standing water – yuck! Also, don't forget to check local building codes before you start. Skipping this step can lead to issues later on. Finally, trying to DIY complex parts like plumbing or subfloor prep when you’re not experienced can lead to bigger problems. Sometimes it's just better to bring in an expert who deals with these details every day. We’re here in the greater Denver area to help ensure your walk-in shower is installed right the first time, preventing those frustrating errors.",
